## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a modular, latency-aware prompt routing flow in an edge/cloud context. It requires turning a user goal into a module selection, a concise execution plan, and a concrete payload while considering safety and edge cases.

## Key Concepts
- Prompt routing and modular design
- PII redaction and latency constraints
- Edge-case handling and fallbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tiny router sketch
function routePrompt(req){
  const intent = req.intent||'';
  const data = req.data_sensitivity||'';
  const latency = req.latency_budget||Infinity;
  if(intent.includes('summary') && data==='PII' && latency<=1000){
    return {module:'Summary-Builder', plan:['fetch','redact','summarize'], payload:{regions:req.regions||['us-east','us-west'], redact:true}};
  }
  return {module:'Data-Extractor', plan:['extract'], payload:{}};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this for latency budgets and safety guards?
- How would you extend to handle parallel modules and partial results?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design stable prompts across models and languages with guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- Prompt contracts, per-model templates, and intent extraction
- Drift testing and edge-case handling for ambiguity
- Guardrails and multilingual normalization
- Minimal prototype demonstration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal prototype sketch
function routePrompt(userInput, context) {
  const templates = {
    en: { default: 'Template_EN' },
    fr: { default: 'Template_FR' }
  };
  const model = context.model || 'default';
  const lang = context.lang || 'en';
  const chosen = (templates[lang] && templates[lang].default) || templates['en'].default;
  const finalPrompt = chosen + '\n' + userInput;
  return { template: chosen, finalPrompt, guardrail: 'none' };
}
```

